        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep bounded exec output UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nBounded exec output used raw UTF-16 string cuts in several paths. When a cut landed between an emoji's surrogate halves, background completion notifications, retained poll output, or approval follow-ups could contain an invalid dangling surrogate that transports render as a broken character.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix applies the existing `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` contract at the owner boundaries:\n\n- the shared exec `tail()` helper now makes suffix cuts safely;\n- aggregate and pending output retention reuse that safe suffix rule and keep character accounting aligned with the actual retained string;\n- the final notification prefix uses `truncateUtf16Safe` before its existing ellipsis;\n- node approval follow-ups reuse the same shared safe tail as the gateway path.\n\nThis removes the remaining raw cuts in the bounded exec-output surface without changing process execution, approvals, routing, permissions, transport behavior, ASCII output, or the existing caps.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong exec output no longer shows a broken character when an emoji lands exactly at a retention or notification boundary. Polls and node/gateway approval follow-ups preserve valid UTF-16, while long notification snippets remain bounded and retain their existing ellipsis behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact prepared head: `ef5683f7598734d59e779d8b0f15deeca9863080`, rebased onto `06fbd84d2b1a61c665f39f7da633df0157d03ed8`.\n\nSanitized direct-AWS proof on the identical seven-file change before the final mainline-only rebase used public networking, no Tailscale, no hydration, and only the `CI` environment variable on lease `cbx_5778b593a277` (`brisk-krill`), head `e0e1112dfabcde4ae1eb52c3cf8ba783016ae4b4`:\n\n- [run `run_4afe631a2a0c`](https://crabbox.openclaw.ai/portal/runs/run_4afe631a2a0c)\n- `pnpm test src/agents/bash-process-registry.test.ts src/agents/bash-tools.exec-runtime.test.ts src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-node.test.ts packages/normalization-core/src/utf16-slice.test.ts`\n- 4 files and 115 assertions passed: registry 10, runtime 38, node follow-up 49, UTF-16 helper 18.\n\nSecretless exact-head fork CI run `28768587139` independently passed:\n\n- `bash-process-registry.test.ts`: 10 tests\n- `bash-tools.exec-runtime.test.ts`: 38 tests\n- `bash-tools.exec-host-node.test.ts`: 49 tests\n- `bash-tools.exec-host-gateway.test.ts`: 53 tests\n- `utf16-slice.test.ts`: 18 tests\n\nA broader AWS run passed 149/150 assertions. Its only failure was an untouched gateway allowlist test that expects `/usr/bin/head`; the AWS image resolves that binary as `/usr/lib/cargo/bin/coreutils/head`. The exact-head GitHub lane passed all 53 tests in that file.\n\nFresh AutoReview on prepared head `ef5683f7598734d59e779d8b0f15deeca9863080` reported no actionable findings. `git diff --check` passed. Exact-head hosted CI run [`28769705252`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28769705252) completed successfully with no failed checks.\n\nNo live channel round-trip was run. The focused runtime tests exercise the exact strings handed to system-event delivery and approval follow-up before transport.\n\nAI-assisted: implementation and validation used AI assistance; all cited commands and run identifiers are real.\n",
        "branch": "fix/exec-notify-utf16-boundary",
